    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed, mini.operators\n\n### Description\n\n`mini.bracketed` seems to provide most functionality of tpope's `vim-unimpaired`. I'm still missing the `[<space>` and `]<space>` commands to insert a new line before or after the current line. Given the scope of `mini.bracketed`, these mappings might fit better into `mini.operators`. Are these bindings already available somewhere? Or is it planned to add them?",
